    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_7",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Neurosyphilis is an infection of the brain or spinal cord caused by the spirochete \"Treponema pallidum\". It usually occurs in people who have had chronic, untreated syphilis, usually about 10 to 20 years after first infection and develops in about 25%–40% of persons who are not treated. The United States' Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) advises that neurosyphilis can occur at any stage of a syphilis infection.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
